# The Shire to Bree

**Description:** A dangerous journey through the Old Forest to the Prancing Pony.
**Category:** Middle-earth
**Color:** #00FF00
**Character:** Frodo
**ID:** lotr

---

## Waypoints

### Hobbiton
📍 -37.868, 175.680
📏 250m

Your adventure begins at Bag End. Gandalf's fireworks still echo in memory as you leave the only home you've ever known, the Ring heavy in your pocket.

---

### The Ivy Bush
📍 -37.869, 175.682
📏 450m

A small tavern on the Bywater road. Daddy Twofoot spins tales of goblins and giants here, though few hobbits believe them anymore.

---

### The Green Dragon
📍 -37.872, 175.685
📏 3500m

A quick pint for the road? Sam and Pippin cast longing looks at the inn, but the Black Riders are already searching the shire. You must press on.

---

### The Three-Farthing Stone
📍 -37.900, 175.700
📏 7500m

The geographic center of the Shire. You pause to look back at the rolling green hills. You are leaving the known world behind.

---

### Maggot's Farm
📍 -37.950, 175.750
📏 22000m

Mushrooms and dogs! You take a shortcut through the crops to avoid the road, but Farmer Maggot catches you. Luckily, he offers a wagon ride to the ferry.

---

### Bucklebury Ferry
📍 -38.100, 175.900
📏 7200m

The Brandywine River flows swift and deep. You leap onto the ferry just as hooves thunder on the pier behind you. The Nazgûl screech in frustration.

---

### Crickhollow
📍 -38.150, 175.950
📏 12000m

A quiet house where you leave a decoy behind. Fatty Bolger stays to keep up appearances, while you vanish into the wild.

---

### The Hedge Gate
📍 -38.250, 175.975
📏 48000m

A narrow tunnel through the High Hay, the great hedge that guards Buckland from the Old Forest. You push through into the darkness beyond. The gate clicks shut behind you.

---

### The Old Forest
📍 -38.685, 176.070
📏 15000m

The trees whisper and shift around you. Paths twist and turn, herding you toward the Withywindle. Old Man Willow traps Merry and Pippin in his roots until a strange singing fills the air.

---

### Tom Bombadil's House
📍 -38.780, 175.950
📏 25000m

Goldberry sets the table and Tom sings songs older than the world. For two nights you rest here, safe from all darkness. Tom sends you on your way with a rhyme to remember.

---

### The Barrow-downs
📍 -38.900, 175.800
📏 75000m

Cold fog rolls over the ancient burial mounds. A wight drags you into the earth. You call for Tom, and his song cracks the barrow open. He arms you with blades of Westernesse.

---

### The East Road
📍 -39.500, 175.550
📏 95000m

You rejoin the Great East Road at last, the ancient highway running from the Grey Havens to the Misty Mountains. Civilization feels close, but the road is exposed and the Riders could be anywhere.

---

### The Chetwood
📍 -40.300, 175.100
📏 70000m

A tangled forest of oak and chestnut on the outskirts of the Bree-land. The trees here are ordinary—no malice in them—but you keep your guard up all the same.

---

### Staddle
📍 -40.900, 174.900
📏 50000m

A small village of hobbits on the southeastern slopes of the Bree-hill. Smoke rises from round doors set into the hillside. You are nearly there.

---

### Bree
📍 -41.300, 174.788

The Prancing Pony's warm light beckons. Strider waits in the shadows, and your fellowship begins to form. The real journey lies ahead.

---
